# decision Release-channel manifests come from immutable assets {#channel_checksums}

`release-channels.py` renders the Homebrew formula and Scoop manifest from the `checksums.txt`
already attached to the named GitHub Release. A recovery rebuild is never a checksum source:
GoReleaser archives rebuilt from the same tag can have different bytes, while their published
URLs still resolve to the original immutable assets. Missing expected archive names or malformed
SHA-256 values are fatal; never guess, reuse a rebuild hash, or overwrite a release asset.

# decision Homebrew uses a formula until macOS artifacts are notarized {#homebrew_quarantine}

An unsigned, non-notarized macOS binary downloaded as a cask is assigned
`com.apple.quarantine`; macOS Gatekeeper rejects its first launch (observed as exit 137 after a
successful checksum-verified install). The tap therefore publishes `Formula/git-a2a.rb`. The
formula installs the already checksum-verified release binary and then removes quarantine from
that one installed file before its `test` invokes `git-a2a --version`. Do not publish a cask or
remove this targeted step until the release pipeline signs and notarizes both macOS binaries.
Quarantine removal is conditional: probe that exact attribute first and delete it only when
present. `xattr -d` returns nonzero when the attribute is absent, so an unconditional call makes
a repeat install fail even though there is nothing to clean. The absence case must remain a
successful, idempotent installation.

# invariant Channel output is deterministic and self-testing

Given the same tag and `checksums.txt`, the renderer writes identical bytes. Formula URLs and
Scoop URLs name the tag-specific archives; every emitted hash is looked up by that exact archive
name. The formula test must execute the installed binary and the Scoop manifest must preserve
separate amd64 and arm64 hashes.

# decision Package-manager repositories are shared collections

`neprel/homebrew-tap` and `neprel/scoop-bucket` are author-level repositories that may publish
many unrelated tools. git-a2a release automation owns only `Formula/git-a2a.rb` in the tap and
`git-a2a.json` in the bucket. It must preserve their general README, metadata, every other
formula or manifest, and the stable user-facing repository names; never reposition either
repository as dedicated to git-a2a.

# decision Manifest reference is compiled from HINT and schema {#manifest_reference}

`gen-reference.py` invokes `hint spec`, reads the `spec` data-structure/field blocks, and joins
them with `spec/schema/a2amodule.schema.json` in schema order. Its fixed route table maps schema
objects to their normative HINT entity ids; it contains no independent field descriptions.
Generation fails when either source has a field the other lacks. The committed
`docs/manifest-reference.md` is deterministic, and `make docs-check` plus CI fail when it is
stale. Python standard library only; do not add a documentation generator dependency.
The compiled stream is XML-like but normative prose may contain literal angle-bracket placeholders
inside backticks, so parse only the compiler-owned `data_structure` and `field` tag boundaries;
feeding the entire stream to a general XML parser would reject valid HINT prose.
On Windows, npm exposes the compiler through a `hint.cmd` shim; Python `CreateProcess` cannot
execute that shim by the bare name. Invoke it through `cmd.exe /d /s /c hint spec` on Windows
only. POSIX invokes `hint spec` directly and never adds a shell.
Open and closed manifest vocabularies are compiler-owned `data_definition` tables in
`spec/_.hint`. The generator injects those tables into every applicable field entry and fails on
unresolved “See term”, “See root decision”, or “documented below” wording. Reference terms and
root decisions are expanded to their normative bodies rather than leaving navigation instructions
in the generated document.
`sync-skill.py` treats `skills/git-a2a/SKILL.md` plus the three canonical docs as inputs. It makes
byte-identical full reference and static-site trees plus the Stripe-style
`/.well-known/skills/index.json`; the separately embedded setup copy stays thin at exactly
`SKILL.md` plus `references/README.md`, and only its metadata version is synchronized. Check mode fails on version or copy drift. Skill frontmatter
`metadata.version` must equal `internal/version/VERSION`. Generated text is written as explicit
UTF-8 bytes with LF endings so byte checks have the same result on Windows and POSIX.
`gen-reference.py` also writes a byte-identical copy under `internal/reference/`; Go embeds that
generated artifact for `git-a2a explain`. Check mode fails if either the public guide or embedded
copy differs from the same rendered source after platform newline normalization; the generator
itself and the committed Git blobs remain explicit UTF-8 with LF endings.
The same run extracts `contact_kinds` into `docs/contact-kinds.md`, generates the site's concise
`llms.txt` map and `llms-full.txt` canonical-document concatenation, and checks local Markdown
targets across README, spec, and docs. These files are outputs, never separately authored sources.

# decision Transcript captures the status table byte-for-byte

The transcript generator stores command stdout without trimming, collapsing, or reformatting and
embeds the same bytes in JSON and the no-JavaScript HTML fallback. Status header changes, including
the conditional presence of the `VENDOR` column, must be regenerated from the fixture rather than patched by hand. The fixture
comparison normalises only the resolved commit hash; tabwriter spacing and every other byte remain
an acceptance check.

# test Release channels

- A fixture `checksums.txt` drives both manifests and all four hashes appear in their correct
  architecture entries.
- A missing expected archive fails instead of emitting a partial manifest.
- A recovery dispatch skips GoReleaser's Homebrew/Scoop publishers, downloads the immutable
  release checksums, removes any obsolete cask, and commits only changed formula/bucket files.
- A real Homebrew install has no quarantine attribute and prints `channel=brew` on first launch.
- Reinstalling when the binary has no quarantine attribute succeeds and still passes `brew test`.
- The Windows amd64 Scoop archive hash matches the manifest and its executable prints
  `channel=scoop` under Wine on an amd64 host or a Windows runner. Do not treat Wine under amd64
  QEMU on Apple Silicon as a valid gate: `scottyhardy/docker-wine` aborts in
  `anon_mmap_fixed` before the executable starts because of the emulated host page layout.
